  ],
  "notes": "Euphemia Allen, The Celebrated Chop Waltz (1877), solo version, first section bars 1-16 up to Fine. RH plays the composer's dyads in the original register: F5/G5, E5/G5, D5/B5, C5/C6, with the cadence C5/C6-G5-E5 then C5. Old repo had only the lower note of each dyad, an octave too low, and was 8 bars long. Lowering the RH an octave would collide with the LH chords, so the original register is kept. LH simplified for the level: the composer's bass note on beat 1 (G3 or C3), then only the top two notes of the original 3-note chords (D4/F4 for G7, C4/E4 for C) on beats 2-3. Final C5 and C3 held for the full bar; the composer also doubles C4 in the LH at the end, which is dropped here. Validation exceptions: the beginner level (tag level-3) cannot fit the original dyads (range, 2 notes per hand, spans up to an octave); the beginner/level-3 tag is too low for the real piece."
}
